# 22. Tourism Without Productivity Theater

VibeTour should avoid fake metrics.

Do not tell users:

“You traveled 84 miles because you wrote 847 lines.”

Lines written are not meaningful productivity.

Journey progression should be intentionally abstract.

The experience represents productive momentum, not a scientific measurement of output.

---

# 23. Idle Experience

Idle time presents an opportunity rather than a failure.

Short inactivity:

vehicle continues moving.

Medium inactivity:

slows naturally.

Long inactivity:

pulls into an interesting location.

Examples:

- viewpoint
- roadside café
- scenic turnout
- gas station
- hotel
- mountain overlook
- beach parking area

Returning to work resumes the journey.

This creates natural moments of visual reward.

