# 34. North-Star Moment

The product has succeeded when this happens:

A developer starts work intending to complete a feature.

They select:

**Tuscany — Florence to Siena.**

For the next two hours they code, talk to an agent, run tests and review changes.

Occasionally they look up and realize vineyards, villages and hills have been passing by.

Their tests pass.

The feature is complete.

The sun is setting.

The vehicle enters Siena.

A subtle card appears:

**ARRIVED**

**Feature complete.**

No points explosion.

No cartoon confetti.

Just the feeling:

> *I built something — and went somewhere.*

That should be VibeTour.

One thing I’d prioritize even more after writing this: **VibeTour probably starts as a second-screen product, not an IDE replacement.** That lets the travel experience be spectacular immediately while you gradually earn the right to take over more of the actual coding UI.


